# Line endings.
#
# `journal.ndjson` is the guild's durability record and the ONE artifact git carries for
# the board (plugins/guild/docs/v5-design.md §2.3). Every reader of it parses positionally
# and requires each line's last byte to be `}`, so a CR before the newline makes the whole
# file unreadable — and an unreadable journal used to be indistinguishable from an empty
# one: `guild rebuild` produced an empty board and `guild journal compact` overwrote the
# file, both at exit 0.
#
# The CLI now refuses on both paths, but a refusal is a worse outcome than never getting
# the CRLF in the first place. `-text` means: never convert, in either direction, whatever
# core.autocrlf or a `* text=auto` rule says. The pattern has no slash, so it matches at
# any depth — this repo's own .guild/, and any fixture or test workspace under it.
journal.ndjson -text

# The spool files (.guild/spool/<TASK-ID>.ndjson, and the rejected/ copies that are the
# only record of an agent line the drain could not import) are parsed the same way.
*.ndjson -text

# Shell is run by bash 3.2 on macOS and by CI on Linux. A CR at end of line turns a
# heredoc terminator into a syntax error, and `scripts/guild` has no extension.
*.sh text eol=lf
plugins/guild/scripts/guild text eol=lf
